 ## Overview
-SplatQ is a post-training pruning framework for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that addresses the spatial quality imbalance and ignored joint deletion effects of global Top-K methods [S1, unofficial]. It partitions Gaussians into size-limited blocks based on spatial and appearance similarity, allocates retention quotas to balance regional budget, and uses a Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) model to jointly select Gaussians within each block, thereby accounting for pairwise interactions and overlapping contributions [S1, unofficial].
